   "transcript": [
    "The village is rattled. Everyone's jumpy — eyes on the treeline.",
    "⚔ THE BIG BEAST! You're on your own.",
    "Turn-based now. Tap a tile to move — speed is squares. Then act.",
    "The woods go silent — not quiet. Silent. Like the world holding its breath. The pack is already moving. They go quiet before the rush. If the birds stop, they're already moving.",
    "You catch fragments by the fire — Autumn telling Viola about you. The retelling is already better than the event.",
    "🚶 Greta is back — found Autumn.",
    "◈ Something in Jorge's eyes has changed. They've seen enough out there to stop being afraid of the dark.",
    "— NIGHT — Camp. Rest — or risk the dark.",
    "Night. The treeline is just a sound now. The fire is the whole argument against it.",
    "The door is quiet. Haven breathes.",
    "🛟 Autumn stands up by the fire. \"Nobody's saying it, so I will: we need a plan, tonight. Here's what we CAN do — pick one, maybe two, but everything costs something.\"",
    "\"There's hurt to tend and bellies to fill. Triage for the hurt, rations to stretch what's left, or a hard hunt to replace what we lost.\""
   ]
